<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">University of Chicago</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1890</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The University of Chicago is a private research university in Chicago, founded in 1890 with funding from John D. Rockefeller. Its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oriental-institute">Oriental Institute</a>, established by James Henry Breasted in 1919, has led excavations across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/near-east">Near East</a>. The university sponsored Edgar Banks's dig at Adab in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a> in 1903–1905 and, from 2006, excavations at Zincirli in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>, the site of ancient Sam'al.</p></div>
